<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>CWC 1 Eve of Destruction, 1995</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;Eve of Destruction&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Duration: 24 Hours&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Date: November 5, 1995&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;IMG src="http://www.skytrailer.com/images/F-15As_525TFS_36TFW_Cochem_1977.jpg"&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;On October 28, 1995, an explosion&amp;nbsp;in the Baku Metro in Baku,&amp;nbsp; Azerbaijan SSR, killed nearly 300 people.&amp;nbsp; The Soviet Union and her allies blamed western agents for the attack, and promised that a harsh response would be met to the West.&amp;nbsp; The West once again didn't take this threatening of an attack seriously.&amp;nbsp; What happened on October 31, 1995, changed the world forever.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The first of the many attacks that day was a bomb that ripped through the arrivals section of Charles De Gaulle International Airport in Paris, leaving 70 dead and over 200 injured.&amp;nbsp; The next bomb went off on an Iran Air&amp;nbsp;Boeing 707&amp;nbsp;from Tehran to Damascus, leaving 168 passengers and crew dead.&amp;nbsp; The next attack was a SAM launch at a Lufthansa Boeing 747 taking off from Frankfurt Airport, leaving over 100 dead and over 200 injured.&amp;nbsp; The next bomb went off in Washington D.C. on the George Washington Memorial Bridge, killing 20 and injuring 39.&amp;nbsp; Another attack happened in Washington D.C. outside the United States Capitol Building, leaving a congressman seriously injured, but nobody was killed.&amp;nbsp; The last attacks were in the San Francisco Bay Area, killing close to 600 people combined and closing several bridges and roads entering the city.&amp;nbsp; All in all, close to 800 people perished that day in the attacks.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;NATO almost immedietly turned its head towards the thought of KGB sleeper agents and Spetsnaz units.&amp;nbsp; The Soviets denied responsibility.&amp;nbsp; NATO began to call up reserve divisions in Western Europe and Norway as the Soviets increased maritime patrols, combat air patrols, and naval activity.&amp;nbsp; On the night of November 4, 1995, 3 United States recon satellites lost contact with their controllers on the ground.&amp;nbsp; The United States President George H.W. Bush issued an executive order federalizing 150,000 Reserve and National Guard troops just a few hours later.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Just minutes after President Bush gave this order, Soviet artillery came crashing down in the Fulda Gap, Northern Norway, the plains of Northern Germany, and Austria.&amp;nbsp; The Third World War had begun.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Author's note: This is a VERY LARGE and complex scenario.&amp;nbsp; Many missions have been set up.&amp;nbsp; In terms of game speed, the more enemy units you kill the faster the scenario becomes.&amp;nbsp; This is my first scenario I have released so please be very lenient with any errors.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Created by B52H&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
